            <ArticleTitle>Personal view: In-hospital patient management strategies after acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>640-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The coronary patient after the striking experience of a myocardial infarction faces a completely new situation possibly affecting lifestyle, occupation and life expectancy. A dedicated post-infarction diagnostic strategy for the evaluation of the individual risk of suffering from a future coronary event, or of dying, requires profound knowledge of the impact of medical and surgical therapies on the survival rate and on the quality of life after infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
